  "verbalization": "Dexfosfoserine appears to have a mechanistic link to G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1 through the pathway involving Quisqualic acid. The evidence suggests that Dexfosfoserine inhibits Phosphoribosylformylglycinamidine synthase, which in turn targets Quisqualic acid, and Quisqualic acid further targets G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1. This pathway is supported by high scores in both visible paths, indicating a plausible biological relationship. The shared target Quisqualic acid is a key mediator in both pathways, suggesting a potential common mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Quisqualic acid as a central node in the regulation of G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1. The evidence supports a mechanistic connection, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Dexfosfoserine in the regulation of cyclin B1.",
